msgstr "Hotel Check-In Samtale"

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/features/RolePlay/scenarios/hotel-check-in.ts:8
msgid "Hotel Check-In"
msgstr "Hotel Check-In"

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/features/RolePlay/scenarios/hotel-check-in.ts:9
msgid "Practice checking into a hotel, confirming your reservation, asking about amenities, and solving common problems at reception."
msgstr "Øv dig i at checke ind på et hotel, bekræfte din reservation, spørge om faciliteter og løse almindelige problemer i receptionen."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/features/RolePlay/scenarios/hotel-check-in.ts:13
msgid ""
"Checking into a hotel usually follows a predictable pattern. The receptionist confirms your identity and reservation, explains the hotel’s services, and gives you access to your room.\n"
"\n"
"Knowing a few key phrases can make the process much easier, especially when you are travelling in a country where you do not speak the local language confidently.\n"
"\n"
"## What You May Need at Check-In\n"
"\n"
"The receptionist may ask you for:\n"
"\n"
"- Your full name\n"
"- A passport or identity document\n"
"- Your booking confirmation\n"
"- A payment card\n"
"- The number of guests\n"
"- Your expected check-out date\n"
"\n"
"You can begin the conversation with:\n"
"\n"
"- “Hello, I have a reservation.”\n"
"- “Hi, I’d like to check in.”\n"
"- “The reservation should be under Alex Dmowski.”\n"
"- “I booked the room through a booking website.”\n"
"- “Here is my booking confirmation.”\n"
"\n"
"If the receptionist cannot find your reservation, stay calm and provide more details:\n"
"\n"
"- “Could you check the booking number?”\n"
"- “I received a confirmation email yesterday.”\n"
"- “The reservation may be under my partner’s name.”\n"
"- “Would it help if I showed you the confirmation?”\n"
"\n"
"## Confirm the Important Details\n"
"\n"
"Before accepting the room, confirm that the reservation details are correct.\n"
"\n"
"You may want to check:\n"
"\n"
"- The room type\n"
"- The number of nights\n"
"- The total price\n"
"- Whether breakfast is included\n"
"- The number and size of beds\n"
"- The check-out time\n"
"- Any additional fees or deposits\n"
"\n"
"Useful questions include:\n"
"\n"
"- “Could you confirm which room type I booked?”\n"
"- “Is breakfast included in the price?”\n"
"- “What time is check-out?”\n"
"- “Is there a security deposit?”\n"
"- “Are there any additional charges?”\n"
"- “Has the room already been paid for?”\n"
"- “Could I have a receipt, please?”\n"
"\n"
"Do not be afraid to ask the receptionist to repeat information:\n"
"\n"
"- “Sorry, could you repeat that?”\n"
"- “Could you speak a little more slowly, please?”\n"
"- “Did you say check-out is at eleven?”\n"
"- “Could you write that down for me?”\n"
"\n"
"## Ask About Hotel Services\n"
"\n"
"Check-in is a good time to ask practical questions about your stay.\n"
"\n"
"### Wi-Fi\n"
"\n"
"- “Is Wi-Fi included?”\n"
"- “What is the Wi-Fi password?”\n"
"- “Does the Wi-Fi work inside the rooms?”\n"
"\n"
"### Breakfast\n"
"\n"
"- “What time is breakfast served?”\n"
"- “Where is the breakfast area?”\n"
"- “Do you have vegetarian options?”\n"
"- “Can I add breakfast to my reservation?”\n"
"\n"
"### Hotel facilities\n"
"\n"
"- “Does the hotel have a gym?”\n"
"- “Is there a place where I can leave my luggage?”\n"
"- “Do you have laundry service?”\n"
"- “Is room service available?”\n"
"- “Is there a restaurant in the hotel?”\n"
"\n"
"### Transport and local information\n"
"\n"
"- “Could you help me call a taxi?”\n"
"- “What is the easiest way to get to the city centre?”\n"
"- “Is there a bus stop nearby?”\n"
"- “Could you recommend a restaurant in the area?”\n"
"\n"
"## Make a Special Request\n"
"\n"
"It is best to make important requests before arriving, but you can also ask at reception.\n"
"\n"
"Common requests include:\n"
"\n"
"- A quiet room\n"
"- A room on a higher or lower floor\n"
"- Two separate beds\n"
"- A larger bed\n"
"- A baby cot\n"
"- An accessible room\n"
"- Extra towels or pillows\n"
"- Early check-in\n"
"- Late check-out\n"
"- A room away from the lift\n"
"\n"
"Useful phrases:\n"
"\n"
"- “Would it be possible to have a quiet room?”\n"
"- “Could I have a room away from the lift?”\n"
"- “Do you have a room on a higher floor?”\n"
"- “Could we have two separate beds?”\n"
"- “Would it be possible to check out later?”\n"
"- “Could you send an extra towel to the room?”\n"
"\n"
"Using “Could I…?”, “Would it be possible…?” and “Do you have…?” makes your request sound polite and natural.\n"
"\n"
"## Handle Common Problems\n"
"\n"
"Sometimes the room is not ready, the booking details are incorrect, or the room does not match what you reserved.\n"
"\n"
"### The room is not ready\n"
"\n"
"- “Do you know when the room will be ready?”\n"
"- “Could I leave my luggage here?”\n"
"- “Could you let me know when I can check in?”\n"
"- “Is there somewhere I can wait?”\n"
"\n"
"### The reservation cannot be found\n"
"\n"
"- “I have a confirmation email. Could you check it?”\n"
"- “Could you search using the booking reference?”\n"
"- “The reservation may be under a different name.”\n"
"- “Could you contact the booking platform?”\n"
"\n"
"### The room is different from the booking\n"
"\n"
"- “I believe I booked a double room.”\n"
"- “My confirmation says that breakfast is included.”\n"
"- “I requested two separate beds.”\n"
"- “Could you check the original reservation?”\n"
"- “Is another room available?”\n"
"\n"
"### There is a problem with the room\n"
"\n"
"- “The air conditioning does not seem to work.”\n"
"- “The room has not been cleaned yet.”\n"
"- “There is a lot of noise coming from the next room.”\n"
"- “The Wi-Fi is not working in my room.”\n"
"- “Could someone take a look at it?”\n"
"- “Would it be possible to change rooms?”\n"
"\n"
"Describe the problem clearly, explain what you expected, and ask for a specific solution.\n"
"\n"
"## Understand Common Receptionist Questions\n"
"\n"
"A receptionist may ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “May I have your name?”\n"
"- “Could I see your passport or ID?”\n"
"- “Do you have your booking confirmation?”\n"
"- “How many nights will you be staying?”\n"
"- “Will you be paying by card or cash?”\n"
"- “Would you like breakfast included?”\n"
"- “Do you need help with your luggage?”\n"
"- “Would you like a wake-up call?”\n"
"- “Do you have any special requests?”\n"
"\n"
"You do not need to give long answers. Clear and direct responses are usually best.\n"
"\n"
"For example:\n"
"\n"
"> “Yes, the reservation is under Dmowski. I’ll be staying for three nights, and I’ll pay by card.”\n"
"\n"
"## A Simple Check-In Conversation\n"
"\n"
"A typical conversation may follow this structure:\n"
"\n"
"1. Greet the receptionist.\n"
"2. Say that you have a reservation.\n"
"3. Give your name and identification.\n"
"4. Confirm your booking details.\n"
"5. Ask about breakfast, Wi-Fi, or check-out.\n"
"6. Make any special requests.\n"
"7. Collect your room key and directions.\n"
"8. Thank the receptionist.\n"
"\n"
"Example:\n"
"\n"
"> **Guest:** Hello, I have a reservation under Dmowski.  \n"
"> **Receptionist:** Certainly. May I see your passport, please?  \n"
"> **Guest:** Of course. Here you are. Is breakfast included in my booking?  \n"
"> **Receptionist:** Yes, it is served from seven until ten.  \n"
"> **Guest:** Great. Could you also tell me the Wi-Fi password?  \n"
"> **Receptionist:** It is written on your key card.  \n"
"> **Guest:** Thank you. What time is check-out?  \n"
"> **Receptionist:** Check-out is at eleven.  \n"
"> **Guest:** Perfect. Thank you for your help.\n"
"\n"
"## Practice Scenario\n"
"\n"
"In this roleplay, you have arrived at a hotel where you already have a reservation. The AI receptionist will ask for your details, explain the hotel’s services, and respond to your questions.\n"
"\n"
"During the conversation, try to:\n"
"\n"
"- Introduce yourself and confirm your reservation.\n"
"- Ask at least two questions about the hotel.\n"
"- Make one polite request.\n"
"- Confirm an important detail by repeating it.\n"
"- Respond to an unexpected issue if one occurs.\n"
"\n"
"Focus on communicating clearly rather than using perfect grammar. A successful check-in is one where both you and the receptionist understand what needs to happen next."
msgstr ""
"At tjekke ind på et hotel følger normalt et forudsigeligt mønster. Receptionisten bekræfter din identitet og reservation, forklarer hotellets tjenester og giver dig adgang til dit værelse.\n"
"\n"
"At kende et par nøglefraser kan gøre processen meget lettere, især når du rejser i et land, hvor du ikke taler det lokale sprog selvsikkert.\n"
"\n"
"## Hvad du måtte have brug for ved indtjekning\n"
"\n"
"Receptionisten kan bede om:\n"
"\n"
"- Dit fulde navn\n"
"- Et pas eller identitetsdokument\n"
"- Din reservationsbekræftelse\n"
"- Et betalingskort\n"
"- Antallet af gæster\n"
"- Din forventede udtjekningsdato\n"
"\n"
"Du kan starte samtalen med:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Hej, jeg har en reservation.\"\n"
"- \"Hej, jeg vil gerne tjekke ind.\"\n"
"- \"Reservationen burde være under Alex Dmowski.\"\n"
"- \"Jeg har booket værelset gennem en bookingside.\"\n"
"- \"Her er min reservationsbekræftelse.\"\n"
"\n"
"Hvis receptionisten ikke kan finde din reservation, forbliv rolig og giv flere detaljer:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Kunne du tjekke reservationsnummeret?\"\n"
"- \"Jeg modtog en bekræftelsesmail i går.\"\n"
"- \"Reservationen kan være under min partners navn.\"\n"
"- \"Ville det være nyttigt, hvis jeg viste dig bekræftelsen?\"\n"
"\n"
"## Bekræft de vigtige detaljer\n"
"\n"
"Før du accepterer værelset, bekræft, at reservationsdetaljerne er korrekte.\n"
"\n"
"Du kan ønske at tjekke:\n"
"\n"
"- Værelsestypen\n"
"- Antal overnatninger\n"
"- Den samlede pris\n"
"- Om morgenmad er inkluderet\n"
"- Antal og størrelse af senge\n"
"- Udtjekningstidspunkt\n"
"- Eventuelle ekstra gebyrer eller depositum\n"
"\n"
"Nyttige spørgsmål inkluderer:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Kunne du bekræfte, hvilken værelsestype jeg har booket?\"\n"
"- \"Er morgenmad inkluderet i prisen?\"\n"
"- \"Hvad tid er der udtjekning?\"\n"
"- \"Er der et depositum?\"\n"
"- \"Er der nogen ekstra gebyrer?\"\n"
"- \"Er værelset allerede betalt for?\"\n"
"- \"Kunne jeg få en kvittering, tak?\"\n"
"\n"
"Vær ikke bange for at bede receptionisten gentage information:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Undskyld, kunne du gentage det?\"\n"
"- \"Kunne du tale lidt langsommere, tak?\"\n"
"- \"Sagde du, at udtjekning er klokken elleve?\"\n"
"- \"Kunne du skrive det ned for mig?\"\n"
"\n"
"## Spørg om hotellets tjenester\n"
"\n"
"Indtjekning er et godt tidspunkt til at stille praktiske spørgsmål om dit ophold.\n"
"\n"
"### Wi-Fi\n"
"\n"
"- \"Er Wi-Fi inkluderet?\"\n"
"- \"Hvad er Wi-Fi-koden?\"\n"
"- \"Virker Wi-Fi inde på værelserne?\"\n"
"\n"
"### Morgenmad\n"
"\n"
"- \"Hvornår serveres morgenmad?\"\n"
"- \"Hvor er morgenmadsområdet?\"\n"
"- \"Har I vegetariske muligheder?\"\n"
"- \"Kan jeg tilføje morgenmad til min reservation?\"\n"
"\n"
"### Hotelfaciliteter\n"
"\n"
"- \"Har hotellet et fitnesscenter?\"\n"
"- \"Er der et sted, hvor jeg kan efterlade min bagage?\"\n"
"- \"Har I vaskeservice?\"\n"
"- \"Er roomservice tilgængelig?\"\n"
"- \"Er der en restaurant på hotellet?\"\n"
"\n"
"### Transport og lokal information\n"
"\n"
"- \"Kunne du hjælpe mig med at få fat i en taxa?\"\n"
"- \"Hvad er den nemmeste måde at komme til centrum?\"\n"
"- \"Er der et busstoppested i nærheden?\"\n"
"- \"Kunne du anbefale en restaurant i området?\"\n"
"\n"
"## Lav en speciel forespørgsel\n"
"\n"
"Det er bedst at komme med vigtige ønsker, før du ankommer, men du kan også spørge ved receptionen.\n"
"\n"
"Almindelige ønsker inkluderer:\n"
"\n"
"- Et roligt værelse\n"
"- Et værelse på en højere eller lavere etage\n"
"- To separate senge\n"
"- En større seng\n"
"- En babyseng\n"
"- Et tilgængeligt værelse\n"
"- Ekstra håndklæder eller puder\n"
"- Tidlig indtjekning\n"
"- Sen udtjekning\n"
"- Et værelse væk fra elevatoren\n"
"\n"
"Nyttige sætninger:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Ville det være muligt at få et roligt værelse?\"\n"
"- \"Kunne jeg få et værelse væk fra elevatoren?\"\n"
"- \"Har I et værelse på en højere etage?\"\n"
"- \"Kunne vi få to separate senge?\"\n"
"- \"Ville det være muligt at tjekke ud senere?\"\n"
"- \"Kunne du sende et ekstra håndklæde til værelset?\"\n"
"\n"
"Brug af \"Kunne jeg...?\", \"Ville det være muligt...?\" og \"Har I...?\" gør din forespørgsel høflig og naturlig.\n"
"\n"
"## Håndter almindelige problemer\n"
"\n"
"Nogle gange er værelset ikke klar, bookingdetaljerne er forkerte, eller værelset svarer ikke til, hvad du har reserveret.\n"
"\n"
"### Værelset er ikke klar\n"
"\n"
"- \"Ved du, hvornår værelset vil være klart?\"\n"
"- \"Kunne jeg efterlade min bagage her?\"\n"
"- \"Kunne du give mig besked, når jeg kan tjekke ind?\"\n"
"- \"Er der et sted, hvor jeg kan vente?\"\n"
"\n"
"### Reservationen kan ikke findes\n"
"\n"
"- \"Jeg har en bekræftelsesmail. Kunne du tjekke den?\"\n"
"- \"Kunne du søge med reservationsnummeret?\"\n"
"- \"Reservationen kan være under et andet navn.\"\n"
"- \"Kunne du kontakte bookingplatformen?\"\n"
"\n"
"### Værelset er anderledes end booking\n"
"\n"
"- \"Jeg tror, jeg har booket et dobbeltværelse.\"\n"
"- \"Min bekræftelse siger, at morgenmad er inkluderet.\"\n"
"- \"Jeg har anmodet om to separate senge.\"\n"
"- \"Kunne du tjekke den oprindelige reservation?\"\n"
"- \"Er der et andet værelse tilgængeligt?\"\n"
"\n"
"### Der er et problem med værelset\n"
"\n"
"- \"Aircondition ser ikke ud til at virke.\"\n"
"- \"Værelset er endnu ikke blevet rengjort.\"\n"
"- \"Der er meget støj fra det næste værelse.\"\n"
"- \"Wi-Fi virker ikke i mit værelse.\"\n"
"- \"Kunne en tage et kig på det?\"\n"
"- \"Ville det være muligt at skifte værelser?\"\n"
"\n"
"Beskriv problemet tydeligt, forklar hvad du forventede, og bed om en specifik løsning.\n"
"\n"
"## Forstå almindelige receptionsspørgsmål\n"
"\n"
"En receptionist kan spørge:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Må jeg få dit navn?\"\n"
"- \"Kunne jeg se dit pas eller ID?\"\n"
"- \"Har du din reservationsbekræftelse?\"\n"
"- \"Hvor mange nætter skal du bo?\"\n"
"- \"Vil du betale med kort eller kontant?\"\n"
"- \"Vil du have morgenmad inkluderet?\"\n"
"- \"Har du brug for hjælp med din bagage?\"\n"
"- \"Vil du have et wake-up call?\"\n"
"- \"Har du nogen specielle ønsker?\"\n"
"\n"
"Du behøver ikke at give lange svar. Klare og direkte svar er normalt bedst.\n"
"\n"
"For eksempel:\n"
"\n"
"> \"Ja, reservationen er under Dmowski. Jeg bliver i tre nætter, og jeg betaler med kort.\"\n"
"\n"
"## En simpel indtjekningssamtale\n"
"\n"
"En typisk samtale kan følge denne struktur:\n"
"\n"
"1. Hils på receptionisten.\n"
"2. Sig, at du har en reservation.\n"
"3. Giv dit navn og identifikation.\n"
"4. Bekræft dine bookede detaljer.\n"
"5. Spørg om morgenmad, Wi-Fi eller udtjekning.\n"
"6. Lav eventuelle specielle forespørgsler.\n"
"7. Modtag din værelsesnøgle og vejledning.\n"
"8. Tak receptionisten.\n"
"\n"
"Eksempel:\n"
"\n"
"> **Gæst:** Hej, jeg har en reservation under Dmowski.  \n"
"> **Receptionist:** Selvfølgelig. Må jeg se dit pas, tak?  \n"
"> **Gæst:** Selvfølgelig. Her er det. Er morgenmad inkluderet i min booking?  \n"
"> **Receptionist:** Ja, det bliver serveret fra syv til ti.  \n"
"> **Gæst:** Fint. Kunne du også fortælle mig, hvad Wi-Fi-koden er?  \n"
"> **Receptionist:** Den står på din nøglekort.  \n"
"> **Gæst:** Tak. Hvad tid er udtjekning?  \n"
"> **Receptionist:** Udtjekning er klokken elleve.  \n"
"> **Gæst:** Perfekt. Tak for din hjælp.\n"
"\n"
"## Træningsscenario\n"
"\n"
"I denne rollespil har du ankommet til et hotel, hvor du allerede har en reservation. AI-receptionisten vil bede om dine detaljer, forklare hotellets tjenester og svare på dine spørgsmål.\n"
"\n"
"Under samtalen, prøv at:\n"
"\n"
"- Introducere dig selv og bekræfte din reservation.\n"
"- Stille mindst to spørgsmål om hotellet.\n"
"- Lave én høflig forespørgsel.\n"
"- Bekræfte en vigtig detalje ved at gentage den.\n"
"- Reagere på et uventet problem, hvis et opstår.\n"
"\n"
"Fokuser på at kommunikere klart snarere end at bruge perfekt grammatik. En vellykket indtjekning er én, hvor både du og receptionisten forstår, hvad der skal ske næste."

